      "writtenOn": "2023-05-11T22:18:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t contain \u0027out\u0027 but it has a PEC computed from \u0027out\u0027 (and value[0] and value[1]). How does anyone who receives \u0027data\u0027 use the PEC?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "8cd39be4f07bfe42e9cb6834ae08f609e9b1b5ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3dea8bc9_3b565cc9",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/drivers/default/src/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380689
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-11T22:42:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, the i2c_emulator (ec/zephyr/emul/emul_common_i2c.c:247) will check if there is a fake that supercedes another emulator (there is). This will transmit the data over a \"pretend wire\", which will be consumed by i2c_controller code (ec/common/i2c_controller.c:374) and will compare the PEC transmitted against the PEC computed and then return an error if there is a mismatch. \n\nIt is the i2c_controller.c that has the corresponding \"out\" because it was the bus-driver in this request phase of the transaction.",
      "parentUuid": "a6e926ff_e35d579f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "8cd39be4f07bfe42e9cb6834ae08f609e9b1b5ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c63ee50_c237792c",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/drivers/default/src/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380689
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-11T22:48:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Talking to Keith... I should probably include this in the comments too... \n\nSpecification p. 37: \nThe PEC is appended to the message as dictated by the protocols in\nSection 6.5. The PEC calculation includes all bytes in the transmission, including\naddress, command and data. The PEC calculation does not include ACK or NACK\nbits or START, STOP or REPEATED START conditions. This means that the\nPEC is computed over the entire message from the first START condition.",
      "parentUuid": "3dea8bc9_3b565cc9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "8cd39be4f07bfe42e9cb6834ae08f609e9b1b5ec",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
