      "writtenOn": "2023-06-06T21:27:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand the question correctly:\n\nDaisuke:\nInvoking `battery_is_charge_fet_disabled()` will go do an I2C read against the emulator for the same register address that\u0027s in `out`, the `fet_reg_addr` So this test is leveraging knowledge of how `battery_is_charge_fet_disabled()` is implemented. Here we don\u0027t need to propagate `out` to the emulator because the same register address in `out` is being used in `battery_is_charge_fet_disabled()`.  \n\nEric is using the pre-existing fake function to respond for the emulator fet register read because the emulator doesn\u0027t know how to PEC.\n\nHe\u0027s probably not adding that functionality because I intend to shift us to the upstream smart battery emulator anyway once it has all the features we want.",
      "parentUuid": "0c63ee50_c237792c",
